---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: "Why use this instead of my car’s navigation?",
    a: "Use your navigation while you drive. A plan is for before you leave: built around your car, adapter, and memberships, with every stop checked with the network and a backup where we can verify one.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a custom plan include?',
    a: 'Charging stops and backups for your car, each fact with its check date. The $39 plan adds battery targets plus food, restroom, and lodging notes. The $79 plan covers several days and overnight charging. We recommend hotels but don’t book them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who reviews a plan before I get it?',
    a: 'A person. Nothing goes out on its own.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When will the plan arrive?',
    a: 'Route Plan and Detailed Plan within 48 hours. Multi-Day or Family within 3 business days. The clock starts once we have payment and your trip details.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I find a plan I already bought?',
    a: 'Go to Find My Plans and enter your checkout email. We send a one-time link. No password or account.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where do the charging numbers come from?',
    a: "Stalls, kW, access, and price come from the network’s own locator. Driver reports from PlugShare, X, and Reddit are labeled as reports. Anything unconfirmed is marked.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What if a fact in my plan was wrong?',
    a: 'If a station fact was wrong on the date we checked it, or we miss the delivery time, you get a full refund. Changes a network makes after that date aren’t covered. Write to admin@evtripreports.com within 14 days of your trip.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I report a wrong stall count or a closed site?',
    a: 'Email admin@evtripreports.com with the stop, the date, and what you saw. A photo helps.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you book hotels, and does any network pay you?',
    a: "No. We don’t book anything, and no charging network pays us.",
  },
];
---
<Base title="FAQ" description="Why a plan is different from in-car navigation, how plans are made and reviewed, where charging facts come from, and the refund rules.">
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="h1">FAQ</h1>
      <div class="faq">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{f.q}</summary>
            <p>
              {f.a.split('admin@evtripreports.com').map((part, i, all) => (
                <>
                  {part}
                  {i < all.length - 1 && <a href="mailto:admin@evtripreports.com">admin@evtripreports.com</a>}
                </>
              ))}
            </p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .faq { margin-top: 32px; border-top: 3px solid var(--ink); max-width: 820px; }
  .faq details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 18px 0; }
  .faq summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .faq p { margin: 12px 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 68ch; }
</style>
